\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen rallies after Japan  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  with first support since 1998\b0\par\par\uc2 1,100 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2022\par 21:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \par         * \par       "We have taken decisive action," says Japan's Kanda \par     \par \par         * \par       Dollar still up 23% despite Japan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par     \par \par         * \par       Sterling, Swiss franc, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Norway\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's crown slide after rate hikes \par     \par \par         * \par       Dollar hits new multi-year high vs sterling, euro\par     \par \par   \par  (New throughout, updates prices, market activity and comments)\par     By Gertrude Chavez-Dreyfuss and Alun John\par        NEW YORK/LONDON, Sept 22 (Reuters) - The Japanese yen soared across the board on Thursday after\par monetary authorities \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to boost the battered \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for the first\par time since 1998, although analysts said Japan may struggle to keep the yen strong.\par     The dollar was last down 1.2% at 142.33 yen. It hit a low of 140.31 after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par having earlier reached a fresh 24-year peak of 145.9 yen. The spread between the day's high and low for the\par pair was the widest since June 2016. \par     North American traders cautiously pushed the dollar higher against the yen after Japan stepped in, but\par for now, few are challenging Japan's action.\par         "The market is nervous," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Steven Englander\f28 \uc2 \f2 , head of global G10 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  research and North America\par macro strategy at Standard Chartered in New York. \par   \par         "There is a risk that Japan becomes a permanent presence in the market for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to be\par successful. Not that Japan has to step in everyday, but the market has to be afraid of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," he\par added.\par   \par     The euro, pound, Swiss franc, the Australian and New Zealand dollars, among others, also plunged against\par the yen. \par     "We have taken decisive action," Japan's Vice Finance Minister for international affairs Masato Kanda\par told reporters, responding in the affirmative when asked if that meant \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Confirmation of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  came just hours after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOJ\f28 \uc2 \f2  decided to maintain low interest rates to\par support the country's fragile economic recovery.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOJ\f28 \uc2 \f2  Governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Haruhiko Kuroda\f28 \uc2 \f2  told reporters the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could hold off on hiking rates or changing\par its dovish policy guidance for years.\par     In contrast, central banks around the world, most notably the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 , are raising rates\par aggressively and the policy divergence has weighed on the yen. \par     However, analysts said Japan can't keep propping up the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on a sustained basis.\par     "Over the next three to six months or possibly even longer, as long as those diverging paths of monetary\par policy are still in place and those differences persist, you'll continue to see a weaker yen," said Brendan\par McKenna, international economist and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wells Fargo Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par     Even after Thursday's moves, the dollar is still up 23.6% against the yen so far this year, on track for\par its largest yearly percentage gain in 43 years.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  BONANZA \par     In a busy day for markets, the pound pared the small advance it had made in London trading after the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2  raised interest rates by 50 basis points. \par     The hike was in line with expectations, although markets had been pricing in a small chance of a larger\par 75 bp move. \par     Sterling was last down 0.2% at $1.1251, not too far from a fresh 37-year low of $1.1213, hit in\par Asia trading. \par     The euro was little changed at $0.9832, recovering from a new 20-year trough of $0.9807 hit\par earlier in the global session.\par     The dollar index, which measures the greenback's value against a basket of six  major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par slipped 0.1% to 111.32, sliding from a 20-year high of 111.81 hit early in the day following the conclusion\par of the Fed's policy meeting on Wednesday. \par      The Fed issued new projections showing rates peaking at 4.6% next year with no cuts until 2024. It\par raised its target interest rate range by another 75 basis points (bps) overnight to 3%-3.25%, as widely\par expected. \par     The dollar was already supported by demand for safe-haven assets after Russian President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vladimir Putin\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par announced on Wednesday he would call up reservists to fight in Ukraine.\par     Separately, the Swiss franc tumbled after Switzerland's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  raised rates by 75 bps, when some\par had talked up the possibility of a full percentage point move. \par     The dollar and euro both climbed roughly 1.2% against the franc, with the greenback last at 0.9783\par francs and the euro at 0.9619 francs. \par     The Norwegian crown eased against the euro and dollar after the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hiked interest\par rates by an expected 50 bps, and signalled a more gradual approach to tightening ahead. \par     The euro was last up 0.5% at 10.2203 crowns, while dollar rose 0.3% to 10.3955.\par         ========================================================\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 3:04PM (1904 GMT)\par  Description      RIC         Last           U.S. Close  Pct Change     YTD Pct       High Bid    Low Bid\par                                               Previous                   Change                   \par                                               Session                                             \par  Dollar index                 111.2800       111.4700    -0.15%         16.325%       +111.8100   +110.4600\par  Euro/Dollar                  $0.9835        $0.9838     -0.01%         -13.47%       +$0.9908    +$0.9807\par  Dollar/Yen                   142.4400       144.1050    -1.16%         +23.72%       +145.8900   +140.3100\par  Euro/Yen                     140.09         141.73      -1.16%         +7.50%        +143.7000   +138.7200\par  Dollar/Swiss                 0.9787         0.9663      +1.30%         +7.32%        +0.9849     +0.9622\par  Sterling/Dollar              $1.1255        $1.1270     -0.11%         -16.76%       +$1.1363    +$1.1213\par  Dollar/Canadian              1.3487         1.3466      +0.16%         +6.68%        +1.3544     +1.3410\par  Aussie/Dollar                $0.6643        $0.6633     +0.18%         -8.58%        +$0.6670    +$0.6574\par  Euro/Swiss                   0.9624         0.9507      +1.23%         -7.18%        +0.9715   