\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-\uc2 Norway  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  to buy more foreign  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  for wealth fund\b0\par\par\uc2 319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 2022\par 11:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds \uc2 Nordea\uc2  comment, more background)\par \par \uc2 OSLO, Aug 31 (Reuters) - \uc2 Norway's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it would sharply increase its purchase of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for its sovereign wealth fund in September, amid a surge in the country's oil and gas revenues.\par \par \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2  plans to exchange 3.5 billion Norwegian crowns ($355.41 million) per day into foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , up from 1.5 billion per day in August, which will in turn be invested abroad by the $1.2 trillion wealth fund, already the world's largest.\par \par \uc2 DNB Markets\uc2  had predicted in advance that \uc2 Norges bank\uc2  would increase the daily purchases to 2.5 billion Norwegian crowns.\par \par \uc2 The crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened on the news, falling to 9.90 against the euro at 0926 GMT from 9.82 just ahead of the announcement.\par \par \uc2 "This large shift points toward a weaker NOK ahead," said \uc2 Nordea Markets\uc2 , adding that the increase in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchase would also alleviate upward pressure on Norwegian interbank interest rates.\par \par \uc2 The crown may also in the time ahead be hit by stock market weakness, said \uc2 Nordea\uc2 , forecasting an exchange rate of 10.3 crowns per euro by year-end.\par \par \uc2 This year's spike in the price of petroleum, Norway's main export, has led to a big inflow of tax revenues that exceeded government spending.\par \par \uc2 Economists have said that a larger purchase of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and thus larger sales volumes of crowns, may weaken the Norwegian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2  says its transactions are conducted for fiscal reasons on behalf of the state, and are not to be regarded as market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2  is western Europe's largest oil and gas producer, with daily output of more than 4 million barrels of oil equivalent. ($1 = 9.8477 Norwegian crowns) (Reporting by Terje Solsvik, Editing by Stine Jacobsen and Gareth Jones) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-8-31T10:35:23.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220831ei8v01bj6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
