\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Norway Foreign Exchange Interventions \highlight\uc2  Unlikely -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,505 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 2020\par 17:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2020, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 1157 ET - \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to act on its recent threat to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to limit the krone's decline in the face of weak oil prices, \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  says. "I think \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2  will not do much more than keep an eye on the development of EUR/NOK as we are still a long way off the levels seen in mid-March," Commerzbank \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst \uc2 Antje Praefcke\uc2  says. "Moreover, there is a risk that it would have to stand up against the market and would gain very little while \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a falling oil price." A weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also helps exporters who are "having a tough time" due to coronavirus. EUR/NOK falls 1.8% to 11.4454 as oil prices recover. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1107 ET - The Polish zloty has much further to fall against the euro due to the impact of coronavirus on the country's economy, \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  says. With Poland's consumer confidence and labor market suffering from restrictions to contain the spread of coronavirus, private consumption could "fall significantly" in the coming months with "negative consequences for the entire economy," Rabobank \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist \uc2 Piotr Matys\uc2  says. "The latest set of data supports our argument that EUR/PLN has not peaked yet and the current period of consolidation marked as a descending triangle will be followed by another leg higher towards the global financial crisis high at 4.9307 over the one to three month horizon." EUR/PLN is last flat at 4.5465. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1105 ET - European leveraged issuance ceased completely in March as efforts to contain the coronavirus pandemic shattered businesses and markets, says \uc2 Moody's Investors Service\uc2  . "March leveraged finance issuance ground to a virtual halt with no bonds issued and only one $45 million loan launched," says the credit rating firm, adding that the lack of issuance reflected a "dramatic reversal" from February's activity. A volume of $10 billion bonds and loans were issued that month after a historic peak of $44 billion in January, it adds.(lorena.ruibal@wsj.com; @lorena_rbal)\par \par \uc2 1056 ET - \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  expects the dollar to appreciate further in coming months, particularly against commodity sensitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Norwegian krone and Canadian dollar following the recent collapse in oil prices. "The chaotic turn in the oil markets indicates likely downward macro pressure that will do more damage in the commodity space, putting pressure on commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," \uc2 BofA\uc2  analysts say. The dollar should benefit from demand for safe haven assets as markets focus on the "massive economic fallout" from coronavirus, they say. \uc2 BofA\uc2  expects USD/NOK to rise to as high as 11.47 this year, up from 10.5470 currently, and USD/CAD to hit a high of 1.55 compared to 1.4018 at present. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1002 ET - The Swedish krona would weaken on a possible interest rate cut by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at its April 28 policy meeting to shield the economy from coronavirus, \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  says. There is speculation that the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  could return to negative rates after data sparked concerns that the economy could this year see the "worst recession since World War II," \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  's \uc2 Jane Foley\uc2  says. "EUR/SEK has been on an upward trend since 2012 and for the most part this will have been welcomed by the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  given soft inflation and the importance of its export sector," she says. "If rates are pushed back below zero, the risk of a further extension of the uptrend will increase." EUR/SEK falls 0.4% to 10.8871. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0827 ET - Treasurys are little changed as extremely poor European economic data is offset by an uptick in oil prices. Traders will be paying attention at 11am when the Treasury Department announces the size of next week's note auctions, as analysts continue to debate how the market will digest increased issuance to finance economic rescue packages. The 10-year yield was recently 0.625% vs. 0.618% Wednesday. (sam.goldfarb@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0820 ET - The Swedish economic sentiment indicator recorded by far the biggest drop ever in April to stand at a record low of 58.6. Consumer confidence plunged to 73.9 from 89.4 and confidence in manufacturing industry dropped too, but could have been worse, says \uc2 Nordea\uc2  . Confidence in the total business sector dropped to 53.1, the lowest reading ever. All in all, sentiment plunged like never before, \uc2 Nordea\uc2  says, adding that a massive drop was expected but it's still painful to see. "The survey indicates a huge drop in GDP and close to a two digit decline. The downturn in 2Q is important, but even more important is for how long the standstill will last."(dominic.chopping@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0818 ET - The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to overcome the likelihood of a higher loss in order to be able to buy 'fallen angels', corporate bonds that have been downgraded to junk status, says \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  . "The one item that might pose an issue to the \uc2 ECB\uc2  is the high risk profile of BB fallen angels and the fact that, unlike repo \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , no haircut protects the Eurosystem from potential losses," says the bank. This might explain why the \uc2 ECB\uc2  didn't announce the inclusion of fallen angels as eligible bonds of its bond purchase programmes, though it will accept 'fallen angels' as collateral for banks to access ultra-cheap loans, it says.(lorena.ruibal@wsj.com; @lorena_rbal)\par \par \uc2 0816 ET - The eurozone composite purchasing managers index plunged to a new record low of just 13.5 in April, confirming that an unprecedented contraction in gross domestic product is occurring, says \uc2 Simon Wells\uc2  , chief European economist at \uc2 HSBC\uc2 . This sharp decline means a big downside risk to \uc2 HSBC\uc2  's forecast of GDP falling 11% in the second quarter. "Whatever the magnitude of slump, what is more important is the shape of the recovery and how quickly activity bounces back," Wells says. \uc2 HSBC\uc2  expects April to be the trough in European PMIs. As lockdowns are eased in some countries and exit strategies are discussed, some firms should see rising output in May, he says. (maria.martinez@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0815 ET - Metzler revises its forecasts for the year-end levels of 10-year German Bund and the 10-year \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields. The coronavirus "has led to a downright crash of global economic activity, to unprecedented measures by the major central banks and to massive market distortions," Metzler says. In view of the pandemic, the economic consequences and the question of how to finance the costs incurred, it has adjusted yield forecasts. Metzler now sees the year-end level of the 10-year German Bund yield at -0.60%, compared with its previous forecast of -0.80%, and it sees the U.S. 10-year Treasury yield at 0.5% at year-end, down from its previous forecast of 1.2%. The 10-year German Bund yield trades at -0.416%, while the 10-year \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yield trades at 0.624%, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  . (emese.bartha@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0811 ET - \uc2 Hungary's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to keep interest rates on hold at its April 28 policy meeting after unexpectedly raising lending rates earlier this month to shore up the forint, \uc2 TD Securities\uc2  says. "We think further tightening remains purely a function of EUR/HUF performance," TD strategist Izidor Flajsman says. "The higher the pair, the greater the odds of new hikes of short-term rates." If EUR/HUF tops 365, a deposit rate rise "would not be too much of a surprise." The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on April 7 raised its overnight and one-week collateralized loan rates to 1.85% from 0.9% and launched bond-buying and lending programs. EUR/HUF rises 0.2% to 357.706, having earlier reached a two-week high of 358.5825, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2 . (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0807 ET - The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  's decision to relax collateral rules for high-yield corporate debt increases the likelihood that this paper will become eligible for purchase under the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bond purchase program, says \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  . "We now think there is a 2/3 probability that BB fallen angel bonds that respect the collateral rules will be included as eligible paper for both the Corporate Sector Purchase Program and the Pandemic Emergency Purchase Programme, possibly as early as next week's \uc2 ECB\uc2  meeting." The \uc2 ECB\uc2  said it would allow banks to maintain their access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ultra-cheap liquidity during the current crisis by using bonds that have been downgraded to junk as collateral. This would effectively shield the financial system from a wave of credit rating downgrades.(lorena.ruibal@wsj.com; @lorena_rbal)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 23, 2020 11:57 ET (15:57 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020200423eg4n003ns\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
