\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Swedish, Norwegian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  seen rebounding from virus crisis\b0\par\par\uc2 589 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 2020\par 06:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * reuters://realtime/verb=Open/url=cpurl://apps.cp./Apps/\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 -polls?RIC=EURSEK= EURSEK poll data\par \par \uc2 * reuters://realtime/verb=Open/url=cpurl://apps.cp./Apps/\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 -polls?RIC=EURNOK= EURNOK poll data\par \par \uc2 By Terje Solsvik and Colm Fulton\par \par \uc2 OSLO/STOCKHOLM, April 3 (Reuters) - The Swedish and Norwegian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are expected to gradually recover from recent weakness against the euro and dollar in the next 12 months following a turbulent start this year, a Reuters poll of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists showed on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Both countries are experiencing unprecedented drops in business activity amid global shutdowns to combat the coronavirus pandemic, and Norway has taken a double hit as the price of oil, its biggest export, has crashed.\par \par \uc2 The Norwegian crown tumbled to all-time lows in mid-March before staging a partial comeback when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  threatened to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time in more than two decades.\par \par \uc2 The Swedish crown similarly hit 11-year lows against the euro and its weakest level in 18 years against the dollar in recent weeks, although it too has recovered some lost ground along with a partial rebound in stock markets.\par \par \uc2 By this time next year, the Swedish crown is predicted to rise to a level of 10.6250 to the euro from 10.9506 currently, the median forecast showed, albeit with forecasts ranging from 10.10 to 11.40 per euro.\par \par \uc2 Nordea Markets\uc2 , which predicted some short-term weakness for the Swedish crown, said the longer term prospects were brighter.\par \par \uc2 "Looking to the second half of this year, if things will have improved and we are past the coronavirus, in such an environment, the Swedish crown should gain some strength," Nordea Chief Analyst Niels Christensen said.\par \par \uc2 With public debt at 43-year lows, the government launched a raft of measures, including subsidies for shorter working hours, tax rebates and loan guarantees, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has poured money into the financial system.\par \par \uc2 The Norwegian crown is meanwhile seen trading at 10.60 to the euro one year from now, up from 11.26 currently and a 20% rise from the all-time low of 13.1678 set March 19.\par \par \uc2 The price of North Sea Brent crude, although still down 60% year-to-date, has risen in recent days amid signs a price war between Russia and Saudi Arabia could come to an end.\par \par \uc2 "Less downside risk to the oil price is likely a key driver of the crown's strength," \uc2 Nordea Markets\uc2  said of the Norwegian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2  has declined to comment on any level it might seek to establish for the Norwegian crown, the most recent movement in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely also driven by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  said in a note to clients.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2  has launched business loans, tax deferment and fiscal spending worth at least 360 billion Norwegian crowns ($35 billion) to aid the economy, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  slashed its benchmark interest rate to record lows.\par \par \uc2 Ultimately, the duration of coronavirus lockdowns and their impact on the global economy could be key also to the Nordic \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We can easily get a new wave of market unrest and if so, smaller \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will suffer," \uc2 Nordea\uc2 's Christensen said.\par \par \uc2 (Other stories from the global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  poll: )\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 10.2898 Norwegian crowns)\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Simon Johnson in Stockholm; Polling by Khushboo Mittal, Indradip Ghosh and Sujith Pai in Bengaluru; Editing by Chris Reese) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-4-3T05:05:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200403eg4300jd9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
