\par\par \b \uc2 Norwegian Krone Soars on First Signs of Market  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  in Over 20 Years\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anna Hirtenstein \par \uc2 500 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2020\par 15:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2020, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 The Norwegian krone posted its biggest daily gain in over a decade, as analysts point to likely market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The krone rose 5% against the dollar and 4.6% against the euro on Tuesday. It traded at 11.09 kroner to $1, rising the most in a day since March 2009.\par \par \uc2 According to Magne Ostnor, an \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at DNB Markets, the move was likely an indication that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2  said last week that it was considering purchases of Norwegian kroner due to the recent high levels of volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 This would be the first time the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought kroner since 1999. At that time, Norway had an exchange rate target to the euro and would buy and sell kroner to keep the value within a set band. Several central banks regularly trade their own \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain a certain valuation, including the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  and the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2  has historically shied away from moves to prop up its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , despite frequent volatility as a result of oil price fluctuations. Norway is Western Europe's biggest energy exporter. The krone is currently the worst performing of all G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , having lost more than a fifth of its value against the dollar since the beginning of the year.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been hit by a combination of a 54% reduction in the price of benchmark Brent crude since the beginning of the year and investors' preference for holding U.S. dollars above all other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  during market turbulence. The continuing global health crisis from the coronavirus, coupled with an oil price war, has prompted investors around the world to liquidate assets for dollars.\par \par \uc2 Norway's pension funds have been exacerbating the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's plunge by rebalancing their \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedges on their portfolios, selling krone and buying dollars and euros, according to Joachim Bernhardsen, a global macro analyst at Nordea. This action amid the global selloff has reduced liquidity in the market.\par \par \uc2 "If you look back to last week, the market was basically not working," Mr. Bernhardsen said. Bid-ask spreads in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market were as much as four times higher than in normal conditions. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely stepping in to smooth out trading conditions and restore liquidity, he said.\par \par \uc2 However, "it is a very jumpy market and even smaller volumes are moving markets a lot," he said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  has also recently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets with the goal of improving liquidity, opening swap lines with 15 other central banks and providing $1.5 trillion into short-term borrowing through the repurchase market.\par \par \uc2 --Caitlin Ostroff contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Anna Hirtenstein at anna.hirtenstein@wsj.com.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 24, 2020 10:22 ET (14:22 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020200324eg3o002ko\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
