\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Norway \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  says has firm policy against  \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention \highlight\uc2  -paper\b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2014\par 08:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 OSLO, Dec 18 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a firm policy against \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and has no position on where the crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Oeystein Olsen told national daily DN, confirming the bank's stance.\par \par \uc2 The crown has been hit in recent months by the plunge in oil prices and suffered its biggest intraday drop in decades on Monday. It recovered by the end of the day, but is still nearly 10 percent weaker against the euro and 22 percent weaker against the dollar than at the start of the year.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 Norges Bank\uc2  has a clear policy that the interest rate is our tool," Olsen was quotes by the paper on Thursday. "We have a board decision stating that we won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to affect the crown's level."\par \par \uc2 A fifth of \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's GDP is generated by its offshore energy sector and the 45 percent drop in crude prices since June dragged the import weighted crown, the bank's preferred measure, to an all-time-low on Monday.\par \par \uc2 "We had a meeting (on Monday) summing up events and got an assessment of the driving forces," Olsen said. "But we were nowhere near having a crisis meeting."\par \par \uc2 "In a situation where the oil price has fallen as sharply as now, it's obvious that the crown weakening works as a buffer that counters the negative effects on the economy," Olsen said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakness strengthens the competitiveness of Norwegian exporters outside the energy sector.    (Reporting by Terje Solsvik; Editing by Susan Fenton)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-12-21T07:54:54.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141218eaci0070t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
