\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  Bullish On NOK After Strong Local Data\b0\par\par\uc2 135 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 2012\par 15:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 1355 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  takes a bullish view on NOK as recent economic data indicate a remarkably strong domestic environment in Norway. Notes soaring manufacturing PMI, consensus-beating retail sales and falling unemployment figures for recent months. \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has become more inclined to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the strong krone, but rate cuts or policy measures to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  are likely to have only short-term effects, it says. Has a medium-term target of 5.53 for USD/NOK and 7.40 for EUR/NOK. USD/NOK trades at 5.7910 and EUR/NOK at 7.5590. (gustav.sandstrom@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 [ 16-04-12 1355GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1085   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120416e84g000wh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
