\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-Norwegian crown allure intact despite rate cut\b0\par\par\uc2 803 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 07:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Repeats Wednesday story, text unchanged)\par \par \uc2  * Norwegian crown slides after surprise rate cut\par \par \uc2  * Impact seen limited, will not dent the crown's allure\par \par \uc2  * Crown to stay strong vs euro, dollar\par \par \uc2  * But further falls possible vs Swedish crown \par \par \uc2  By Jessica Mortimer and Nia Williams\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 14 (Reuters) - Norway's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fired a warning shot at speculators who drove the Norwegian crown to a nine-year high against the euro, but the country's oil-fuelled growth and safe-haven status mean long-term investors are set to keep buying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  The \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2  cut interest rates by 25 basis points to 1.5 percent, confounding market expectations for no change, and said more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength could prompt further reductions. Its decision hit the crown, which could slip again as short-term traders who had bet on a rise cut their losses. \par \par \uc2  But investors who do not believe the \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation in the way the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  has done, given Norway's still healthy growth outlook, are seen snapping up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at cheaper levels. \par \par \uc2  Even if \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2  did \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time since 1999, it would not have the credibility of the SNB, which has a long track record of determined \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  management. \par \par \uc2  "They (the \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2 ) have done their work for now ... But of course if the oil price stays high and risk appetite is increasing we might see investors eager to buy the Norwegian crown again," said Kyrre Aamdahl, senior economist at \uc2 Den Norske Bank\uc2  in Oslo.\par \par \uc2  The euro surged nearly 2 percent to a one-month high of 7.5925 crowns, taking it well above a recent nine-year low of 7.3927 crowns. The crown lost 2 percent versus the dollar\par \par \uc2 and slid sharply against the Swedish crown. \par \par \uc2  SEB chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Carl Hammer said the euro could rise further, towards 7.60-7.70 crowns, but the bank would look to sell the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on rallies above that level.\par \par \uc2  Analysts said the crown was unlikely to return to its recent highs in the near term. \par \par \uc2  But Norway's strong economy and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's links to oil make it attractive to investors seeking alternatives to the crisis-hit euro, especially with oil prices high. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may struggle to stem further gains given many of the reasons behind the crown's appeal are due to developments abroad which are outside its control.\par \par \uc2  STRONG MESSAGE\par \par \uc2  The bank's decision came as a surprise due to Norway's strong economy and rapidly rising house prices. Analysts said lower rates risked causing a housing bubble, which may fuel speculation the bank will hold off from further rate cuts.\par \par \uc2  However, despite the many reasons to buy the crown, analysts said speculators may be wary given the \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2  had sent a strong message that it was serious about crown strength, and still had room to cut rates further if it needed to.\par \par \uc2  "People will be very careful about buying back the Norwegian crown ... The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stated clearly that they would not hesitate to cut again if the crown were to strengthen substantially once again," said Niels Christensen, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Nordea.\par \par \uc2  Other factors may also weigh on the crown in the coming months.\par \par \uc2  Some analysts warned oil prices risk falling from their current high levels, while SEB's Hammer said Norway may make "substantial" purchases of foreign assets through its oil fund in the second half of this year, which would have a negative impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  CONTRAST WITH SWEDEN\par \par \uc2  The Norwegian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strong concerns about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength contrast with statements made by the Swedish Riksbank, which could prompt a further steep correction in the Norwegian crown versus the Swedish crown.\par \par \uc2  Sweden's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Stefan Ingves said at a rate-setting meeting last month that he expected the Swedish krona to strengthen in the months ahead, minutes of their discussion showed. \par \par \uc2  The Norwegian crown slid as low as 1.1741 Swedish crowns, taking it well below Wednesday's high just below 1.19 and the high of 1.2040 crowns hit on March 8.\par \par \uc2  Traders said buying the Norwegian crown against the Swedish crown had been a very popular trade among long-term investors and it could fall further.\par \par \uc2  "The \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2  is incredibly unwilling to accept further Norwegian crown strength, while the Riksbank has projected euro/Swedish crown to reach 8.50 by year-end (versus 8.9 crowns currently)," SEB's Hammer said. \par \par \uc2  In the longer-term SEB expect the Norwegian crown to fall to 1.10 Swedish crowns or even below, he said. \par \par \uc2 