\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Norway to cut oil money spending in 2013\b0\par\par\uc2 419 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 15:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength an "important consideration" -minister\par \par \uc2 * Sees good prospects for domestic economy\par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes by finance minister)\par \par \uc2 By Gwladys Fouche\par \par \uc2 JEVNAKER, Norway, March 11 (Reuters) - Norway is likely to slash the ratio of oil revenue it uses in the 2013 budget, its finance minister said on Sunday, as prospects for the Norwegian economy outshine Europe's and the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reaches multi-year highs against the euro.\par \par \uc2 Oil-rich Norway, largely sheltered from the global economic crisis, has a spending rule that recommends limiting oil-revenue spending in most years to 4 percent of the value of its $604-billion sovereign wealth fund.\par \par \uc2 "In 2013, if little happens ... we will use significantly less than 4 percent from the oil fund," Sigbjoern Johnsen told reporters ahead of government budget negotiations for next year.\par \par \uc2 "It is important that we hold back on the use of oil money because prospects for the Norwegian economy are good."\par \par \uc2 Cutting the ratio of oil money Norway spends does not necessarily mean it will spend less oil money in absolute terms, however, as the size of the fund may grow.\par \par \uc2 Johnsen said the precise figure would be given in October.\par \par \uc2 "What we can do from the Norwegian government side is to ... use significantly less than 4 percent of the oil money ... And it looks like we will do that in 2012 and 2013."\par \par \uc2 The relative strength of the Norwegian crown against the euro, which makes larges swathes of the country's industry less competitive than foreign manufacturers, was also a significant factor in the setting of next year's state budget, he added.\par \par \uc2 "We have seen a strengthening of the crown over a long time. It is an important consideration when we set the parameters for the budget in 2013."\par \par \uc2 Norway's safe-haven crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a nine-year high against the euro on Monday, helped by a strong economy, high oil prices and the low risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Johnsen repeated the growth of \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's mainland economy, which excludes activity from the energy and shipping sectors, would be somewhat lower than the 3.1 percent the government had anticipated, due to lower expected growth in the rest of Europe.\par \par \uc2 An updated estimate for growth will be given in the revised budget in May, he said.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by David Hulmes)\par \par \uc2 NORWAY-BUDGET/ (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | DA | E | RBN | FN | M | NW | O | OIL | SW | RNP | DNP | PTD | PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120311e83b0006n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
