\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Norway \highlight\uc2  c.bank: No change in  \highlight22\uc2 fx intervention \highlight\uc2  view\b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2009\par 10:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 OSLO, March 27 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it had not changed its view towards \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , one day after Governor Svein Gjedrem said the bank will consider \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Gjedrem did not say anything that we haven't said before. \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2 's view on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has absolutely not changed," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokeswoman Siv Meisingseth told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 In a speech in London, Gjedrem said \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2  will consider \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the crown becomes "out of line", adding this was not necessary at present.\par \par \uc2 The crown swung after the comments, as investors struggled to understand if Gjedrem signalled a new, more hands-on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy after the crown's sharp appreciation in past months.\par \par \uc2 Meisingseth said in addition to changing interest rates, \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2  can buy or sell crowns in the market to influence the exchange rate, although "normally the bank will not use \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ".\par \par \uc2 "Exchange market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , irrespective of whether \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is bought or sold, is not an appropriate instrument for influencing the crown over a longer period," \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2  said on its Web site, detailing its array of monetary policy instruments.\par \par \uc2 "However, \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be appropriate if the crown deviates substantially from the level that the bank judges to be reasonable in relation to fundamentals, and if exchange rate developments weaken the prospect of achieving the inflation target."\par \par \uc2 It said "\b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  may also be appropriate in response to pronounced short-term crown fluctuations when liquidity in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market falls to a very low level."\par \par \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2  said it has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since January 1999.\par \par \uc2 The crown, which some analysts said may become the world's new "safe haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ", fell this week after \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2  cut its main rate by half a point to 2 percent and said borrowing costs may continue to fall to 1 percent in 2009. (Reporting by Wojciech Moskwa; editing by Chris Pizzey)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 NORWAY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|DA|FN|NW|SW|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090327e53r000m8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
