\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Norway \highlight\uc2  cbanker: Wd only  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  if NOK "out of line"\b0\par\par\uc2 By George Matlock   \par \uc2 687 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2009\par 13:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, comments, context)\par \par \uc2 LONDON, March 26 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will only consider \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the Norwegian crown (NOK) if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  becomes "out of line", governor Svein Gjedrem said on Thursday, adding that this is not necessary at present.\par \par \uc2 "Our stated policy is that we may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for liquidity reasons. Another reason would be if the value of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was out of line with fundamentals in the economy and hindered our possibility to reach our inflation target," Gjedrem said at a London presentation of the \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2 's Monetary Policy Report after it cut interest rates by 50 basis points to 2.0 percent on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "When it comes to \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, we have not done that since January 1999," he said, adding that those conditions for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not so far been met.\par \par \uc2 The bank's mandate is to target core inflation of 2.5 percent in the medium term.\par \par \uc2 "We are a very small and open economy. The development in our \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  influences price inflation and the real economy more strongly than in most countries. We have seen large swings in our \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.\par \par \uc2 Gjedrem noted that the Norwegian crown weakened against the euro and the dollar until the end of the fourth quarter, then started appreciating against both. The crown has gained about 10 percent versus the euro this year after reaching all-time lows against the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the end of 2008.\par \par \uc2 "If we did (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), we would communicate it well in advance," he added.\par \par \uc2 Asked by Reuters whether he saw the crown as a safe haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said: "No. With oil prices changing so fast it cannot (be described as a safe haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 )."\par \par \uc2 NO SPACE FOR BOND BUYBACKS, OIS MONEY MARKET\par \par \uc2 Gjedrem said the country's capital market was too small to afford a buyback of fixed income assets of the type carried out by central banks in the United Kingdom or the United States to kickstart stalling economies.\par \par \uc2 "We don't have the kind of market to buy as others do. It is not a very deep domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  (government) bond market, nor for commercial bonds, because most big companies borrow in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as they are so export-orientated," he said.\par \par \uc2 Gjedrem also said there was insufficient liquidity in Norway, which is not a member of the European Union, to establish an OIS market as seen in other countries. He said there was not enough overnight market trading to achieve this.\par \par \uc2 The Overnight Index Swap rates are used as a base line for calculating a spread with three-month interbank offered rates in the money market which is an indicator of the propensity for banks to lend.\par \par \uc2 "The crown market depends on international money markets. When banks lend to each other its via the swaps market. The market is too small to establish that (OIS) sophisticated kind of market," he said.\par \par \uc2 OIL FUND NOT PROVINCE OF FINE-TUNING\par \par \uc2 The $323 billion Norwegian sovereign wealth fund, Europe's biggest shareholder, is in the process of shifting from a policy of investing 40 percent in equities to 60 percent, while reducing its fixed-income component to 40 percent.\par \par \uc2 Yet, last year, the fund lost 633 billion crowns, nearly $90 billion) on investments, posting its weakest return in the 10-year history of the fund, a negative 23.3 percent. [ID:nLB219293]\par \par \uc2 Gjedrem said it was not appropriate to "fine-tune" the fund by putting off a decision to invest more in equities.\par \par \uc2 "We don't try to fine-tune this. A decision was taken to increase the allocation to equities to 60 percent from 40 percent. We have a strategy largely based on indexing," he said.\par \par \uc2 "So we buy a lot when equity prices go down, and not so much when equity prices rise." (Reporting by George Matlock; Editing by Victoria Main)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-NORWAY-GJEDREM (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|DA|FN|NW|SW|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090326e53q001lz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
