\par\par \b \uc2  Norway c.bank to resume  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  buying for oil fund. \b0\par\par\uc2 272 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 11:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  OSLO, March 25 (Reuters) - Norway's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday it was resuming purchases of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for its Petroleum Fund, due to save cash for coming generations, and planned to buy between the equivalent of two to six billion crowns ($255 million-$770 million) in 1999. \par \par \uc2  "Norges Bank will resume market purchases of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the accumulation of capital in the Government Petroleum Fund on March 25," it said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  "Daily purchases will amount to 20 million crowns in March," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. "In special cases Norges Bank may decide not to purchase foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to exchange rate developments." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  suspended purchases of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year for the Fund after a plunge in the price of oil, \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main export. It \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets late last year in a bid to bolster the crown. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would publish daily purchase amounts in crowns for the following month on the last business day of each month at 10 a.m (0900 GMT). \par \par \uc2  "The amount may also be changed after the presentation of the National Budget and the Revised National Budget as a result of new estimates for annual transfers to the fund," it said. \par \par \uc2  The Petroleum Fund, set up for when oil and gas wells run dry next century, totalled 171.8 billion crowns at the end of 1998. \par \par \uc2  ((Alister Doyle, Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41, fax +47 22 42 00 18, oslo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010904dv3p01392\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
