\par\par \b \uc2  Norway foreign min plays down euro-crown link hope. \b0\par\par\uc2 320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 1999\par 10:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  OSLO, Jan 19 (Reuters) - Norwegian Foreign Minister Knut Vollebaek played down hopes on Tuesday of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  deal with the European Union to help bolster the crown, saying it would only make sense if the crown were pegged to the euro. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  accords only make economic sense within fixed rate regimes," he told parliament outlining Norway's policies towards Europe. "The Norwegian fixed rate regime was abandoned in 1992." \par \par \uc2  Prime Minister Kjell Magne Bondevik will visit European Commission President Jacques Santer on Tuesday in Brussels and German Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder in Bonn on Wednesday for talks about non-member Norway's future relationship with the EU. \par \par \uc2  Norwegian opposition parties, which have a majority in parliament, have told Bondevik to investigate possible links between the euro and the crown, which has been weak in recent months due to a fall in the price of oil, Norway's main export. \par \par \uc2  Vollebaek reiterated that Norway, which voted "No" to EU membership in a 1994 referendum, had no plans to change its monetary policy to secure any deal on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the European \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hiked interest rates seven times in 1998 in a vain bid to keep the crown stable against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  before giving up in August and putting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into a virtual float. \par \par \uc2  Norway pegged the crown to the euro's forerunner, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  unit (Ecu) in 1990 until selling pressure forced the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to abandon the system in 1992. \par \par \uc2  Economists see little reason why the EU should offer Norway, led by a government opposed to membership, any concessions. Opposition parties have suggested Norway could get greater access to credit at the ECB to help possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  deals. \par \par \uc2  ((Torbjoern Pedersen, Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41, fax +47 22 42 00 18, oslo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1j066bz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
