\par\par \b \uc2  Europe Focus: No End To Krone's Woes In Sight Until Mid '99 \b0\par\par\uc2  By Stephen Cunningham \par \uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 1998\par 17:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LONDON (Dow Jones)--The Norwegian krone looks set to fall back to its 1998 lows against the Deutsche mark, with little hope of a recovery until the middle of 1999 at the earliest, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Weak commodity prices and the risk of an overheating of the domestic economy have battered the krone in recent weeks. Indeed, some analysts see the mark pushing up to its all-time high of NOK4.7180, reached in mid-October. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Norges Bank, had helped the krone to stabilize into a NOK4.40-4.44 range. But with Brent crude oil futures trading at just under $10 a barrel - a 12 year-low - the krone's prospects look bleak. \par \par \uc2  "A more positive outlook for oil may have to wait for March 1999, when OPEC (Organization of Petroleum Exporting Countries) oil ministers are next skeduled to meet," said Rebecca Patterson, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at J.P. Morgan Securities Ltd. \par \par \uc2  The global economic downturn and unusually warm early winter in North America are expected to keep a lid on demand for commodities prices in the first few months of the year. \par \par \uc2  "Should oil prices continue to weaken into early 1999 as we expect, price-supporting news of production cuts are more likely to emerge from the March meeting," Patterson said. \par \par \uc2  At 1456 GMT, the mark stood at NOK4.5425, down slightly from NOK4.5470 earlier but up from NOK4.5350 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Fears that Norway's economy has been growing too quickly, generating wage inflation, have prompted speculation that the mark could test resistance at NOK4.6000 before revisiting its high. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 10-12-98 \par \par \uc2  1600GMT \par \par \uc2  1089 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917duca01yup\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
