\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Dollar soggy in flows-driven trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 606 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 1998\par 11:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 10 (Reuters) - The dollar fell to a one-month low against the mark in Europe on Thursday and was soft against the yen, undermined by sales from investors adjusting their holdings of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of year-end. \par \par \uc2  Concern about a slowdown in U.S. growth have also prompted some selling, dealers said. The mark, meanwhile, has been underpinned by expectations that European interest rates will remain steady after last week's cut by the 11 nations due to start monetary union in January. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell to a low of 1.6580 marks, its weakest since November 6, when it dropped to 1.6555, an area now eyed as near-term support. \par \par \uc2  "It's driven by flows. There are players unwinding dollar positions ahead of the end of the year," said Audrey Childe-Freeman, economist at CIBC Wood Gundy World Markets. \par \par \uc2  At 0825 GMT the dollar was at 1.6580/90 marks, down from 1.6690/6700 in late European trading on Wednesday. Against the yen it hovered just above a one-month low hit in Asian trading at 116.65, trading at 117.16/26, still down from 118.00/10 late on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said buying of Swiss francs featured in Europe, with dollar/Swiss hitting a one-month low below 1.35 Swiss francs and mark/Swiss at a five-week low of 81.30 centimes. \par \par \uc2  Even though dollar sentiment is bearish, there appeared to be little conviction to kick the dollar much lower through the bottom of its month-old range. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar's early push lower is indicative of the overall mood, but whether there is much follow-through is a moot point as volumes remain very thin," said Tim Fox, chief economist at Standard Chartered. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen recovered from its lows after Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said his comment on Wednesday about \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels did not refer to current market levels. He said Wednesday the U.S. was comfortable with levels at 110-120 yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said another negative backdrop for the dollar was the start of debate in the U.S. House of Representatives on Thursday about whether to remove President Bill Clinton from office for his conduct in the Monica Lewinsky affair. \par \par \uc2  In European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading, the mark surged against the Norwegian crown to a seven-week high just shy of 4.56 crowns. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said speculators felt encouraged to dump crowns amid expectations that \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have abandoned the use of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the crown after benchmark oil prices fell to 12-year lows below $10 earlier this week. Norway is the second biggest oil exporter after Saudi-Arabia. \par \par \uc2  Sterling came under pressure from the weaker dollar/mark but trading was sidelined ahead of an annoucement on interest rates by the Bank of England (BOE) at 1200 GMT. Britain is expected to cut interest rates by 25 or 50 basispoints in response to a flow of depressing economic data. \par \par \uc2  Significant moves in sterling would only happen if the BOE sprung a surprise by either keeping the repo rate steady at 6.75 percent of by an aggressive 75 basis points, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The pound was at 2.7620/30 marks, down from 2.7665/75 marks late on Wednesday but off its low at 2.7578 marks. It was up against the weaker dollar at $1.6634/44, up from $1.6579/89. \par \par \uc2  ((Astrid Zweynert London newsroom + 44 171 542 7792 fax +44 171 542 5293, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926duca02p4m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
