\par\par \b \uc2  Nordic  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: Norwegian Krone Gains Despite Fundamentals \b0\par\par\uc2 282 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 1998\par 10:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Meanwhile, the Norwegian krone has risen to three-month highs\par against the mark. The move has been underpinned by a promise from\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Norway\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market to support the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said investors were also buying krone to cover short\par positions. The short-covering was bolstering the krone despite normally\par bearish macro-economic fundamentals such as sagging oil prices and\par political bickering over next year's draft budget.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  Although the political row could intensify and possibly lead to the downfall of the minority-centrist coalition government, market watchers have been largely sanguine saying fiscal discipline will be ensured no matter which government is in power. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in the Nordic region, the Danish krone and the Finnish markka were little changed against the mark. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 0915 GMT, the following prices were quoted as follows. Comparisons\par are with late trade in the previous European session:\par                 Deutsche mark       ECU Index\par Swedish SEK    4.7335 vs 4.7600   125.45 vs 126.20\par Danish DKK     3.8016 vs 3.8017    -      -\par Norwegian NOK  4.3805 vs 4.3905   107.48 vs 107.68\par Finnish FIM    3.0405 vs 3.0400     -      -\par TCW Index\par  Swedish SEK   128.13 vs 128.78\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The weighted ECU index tracks a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that doesn't\par include the dollar or the yen. A higher index means a strengthening of\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the basket.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Danish krone isn't quoted on a weighted ECU index. Only the\par Swedish krona is quoted on a total, competitive, trade-weighted index.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Chip Cummins; 46-8-545-130-91; ccummins@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 24-11-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0955GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1058 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917dubo01er3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
