\par\par \b \uc2  Nordic  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: Confidence In Norway's Ctrl Bk Boosts Krone \b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 1998\par 16:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Norway's second largest opposition party, the Progress Party, said Tuesday that it is ready to resume negotiations with the country's minority government and the Conservative party, Norwegian media reported Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The Progress party's move followed the government's decision earlier Tuesday to scrap planned tax increases in its original 1999 draft budget, which has been viewed as the main point of contention in the budget talks. \par \par \uc2  "If we're seeing an agreement, we can see the Norwegian krone strengthening in that regard," Unibank's Soerensen said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts, however, point out that underpinning this new political optimism is renewed confidence that \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I think it's no secret that the Norwegian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is satisfied with a strengthening Norwegian krone," Soerensen said. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in the Nordic region, the Danish krone and the Finnish markka were little changed against the mark. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 1515 GMT, the following prices were quoted. Comparisons are with\par late trade in the previous European session:\par                 Deutsche mark       ECU Index\par Swedish SEK    4.7285 vs 4.7600   125.24 vs 126.20\par Danish DKK     3.8018 vs 3.8017    -      -\par Norwegian NOK  4.3885 vs 4.3905   107.67 vs 107.68\par Finnish FIM    3.0405 vs 3.0400     -      -\par TCW Index\par  Swedish SEK   127.78 vs 128.78\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The weighted ECU index tracks a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that doesn't\par include the dollar or the yen. A higher index means a strengthening of\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the basket.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Danish krone isn't quoted on a weighted ECU index. Only the\par Swedish krona is quoted on a total, competitive, trade-weighted index.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Chip Cummins; 46-8-545-130-91; ccummins@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 24-11-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1545GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1058 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917dubo01fy5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
