\par\par \b \uc2  Nordic  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Mixed Vs Mark In Calm Late Trade \b0\par\par\uc2 323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 1998\par 16:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  OSLO (Dow Jones)--The four Nordic \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mixed against the Deutsche mark in calm trade late Thursday afternoon. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In spot trade at 1541 GMT, the mark fetched 3.8019 Danish kroner\par (DKK), down from its intraday peak of DKK3.8026 but unchanged from\par DKK3.8018 late Wednesday.\par    Dealers said mild foreign buying helped the Danish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regain\par the small losses it suffered against the mark after an expected rate\par cut by the Danish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  Earlier in the day, Denmark's Nationalbank trimmed its repo rate and floor discount rate by 25 basis points each to 4.40%, and 4.0%, respectively. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Financial markets had anticipated an easing in monetary policy as a\par normalization following a one percentage point rise in the repo and a 50\par basis point rise in the discount rate in September.\par    The Norwegian krone gained against the mark. a move one dealer\par attributed to krone short-covering. The same trader added that the\par most recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Norway\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may also have\par bolstered the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Indeed, fresh figures showed Norges Bank bought\par a net NOK5.2 billion kroner between Oct.28 and Oct 30, to stem the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's fall.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Looking ahead, dealers argued that continued low oil prices, and an\par unresolved budget situation would cap the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's advance in the\par medium term.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile the Swedish krona slipped against its German counterpart on\par profit-taking, according to dealers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bank of England's 50 basis point repo rate cut to 6.75% hadn't\par much of an impact on the Nordic \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , market watchers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In addition, the market took in its stride the Deutsche Bundesbank's\par decision not to lower interest rates. "Some investors may have wished\par the Buba to cut rates, but no one actually believed it would do so,"\par said a Danish trader.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 05-11-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1554GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1058 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917dub500ubm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
