\par\par \b \uc2  Nordic  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Uptrend In Place; Norway Krone Steady \b0\par\par\uc2 394 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 1998\par 17:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  STOCKHOLM (Dow Jones)--The Norwegian krone (NOK) held on to the higher levels reached early in the session Monday and by the end of European trading it was around 3.7% stronger against the Deutsche mark than its record low of NOK4.7380 reached early Friday. \par \par \uc2  The krone rallied to a high of NOK4.5650 against the mark at the outset of European trading Monday from NOK4.6090 late Friday and after some minor intra-day set-backs it once again returned to these levels reaching NOK4.5620 by 1445 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The initial rally came amid speculation that Norges Bank, \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the krone. That would have been in line with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's statement on Friday that it would once again take an active role via market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decided to let the krone float earlier this autumn the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has continued to weaken away from the bank's desired range between 103 and 105 on the trade-weighted ECU index reaching a high above 115 early Friday. Late Monday the krone was quoted at 111.76 on the index. \par \par \uc2  "If you look at the price performance of the krone since (early) Friday it's easy to make the connection that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been buying, and I suppose that's a fair connection," one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst in Oslo said. Like his colleagues at other banks he didn't wish to confirm whether or not Norges Bank had actually done any buying however. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  which traditionally doesn't comment on day-to-day \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , also refused to comment. \par \par \uc2  "After the initial rally the krone ran out of steam though and the market is now looking for a new catalyst to gain further," said Oeystein Stephansen, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst with SEB in Oslo. "But after such massive strengthening in such a short time it isn't strange to see some consolidation around this levels," he added. \par \par \uc2  Another analyst noted however that a test of resistance around NOK4.54 versus the mark feels more likely amid the current upbeat tone in the market than a fall back to NOK4.60. Both levels are very important for the future direction however, he said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 19-10-98 \par \par \uc2  1508GMT \par \par \uc2  1058 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917duaj009qh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
