\par\par \b \uc2  Nordic  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 :Norwegian Krone Soars Amid Talk Of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 403 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 1998\par 11:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  COPENHAGEN (Dow Jones)--The Norwegian krone (NOK) is sharply higher against the Deutsche mark early Monday in Europe amid market speculation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher. \par \par \uc2  However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  traditionally doesn't comment on day-to-day \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and while dealers said talk of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was rife in the market they were unable to confirm it. \par \par \uc2  At 0853 GMT, the mark was fetching NOK4.5775, down sharply from NOK4.6090 late Friday in Europe and well below its record high of NOK4.7380 early Friday morning. \par \par \uc2  On the weighted inverse ECU \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  index the krone is at 112.00 up from 112.75 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Friday it was resuming its practice of market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and I have no doubt but that it is doing so today," one Oslo based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst said. \par \par \uc2  One head trader said his suspicions of Norges Bank's presence in the market were heightened by sudden krone buying by one particular lender, which he said "is always in front of the pack." He believed this institution, which he declined to name, may have received krone buy orders on behalf of Norges Bank, as it often does when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has business to be done in the market. \par \par \uc2  Though the krone has gained more than 3% against the mark since Friday's all-time low, the Oslo \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst believes the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would like to see the krone appreciate even more. \par \par \uc2  "One should remember that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's goal is to have the krone around 105 on the ECU index," he said. \par \par \uc2  Whether or when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will achieve this depends on oil price developments, he added. \par \par \uc2  Norway is the world's second largest exporter of crude oil and the krone is highly sensitive to oil price fluctuations. \par \par \uc2  "If oil prices rise to around $17 a barrel during the winter then we could see a simultaneous krone strengthening to around NOK4.30 to NOK4.40 against the mark," the analyst said. \par \par \uc2  As to the immediate term, the analyst couldn't offer a range for Monday's krone trading other than suggest that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might try to push the krone below 110 on the ECU index and stronger than NOK4.50 against the mark. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 19-10-98 \par \par \uc2  0910GMT \par \par \uc2  1058 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917duaj008oa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
