\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Norway \highlight\uc2  C.Bank made no  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  Aug 31-Sept 1. \b0\par\par\uc2 149 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 1998\par 12:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  OSLO, Sept 7 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it made no net \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Monday and Tuesday last week. \par \par \uc2  At the end of August, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would suspend use of interest rates and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bolster the crown, which weakened sharply after a plunge in oil prices to 10-year lows. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  statistics showed that so far this year it sold a net 18.24 billion crowns on the foreign exchanges. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has made large overall sales of crowns this year as part of its management of the state's Petroleum Fund, which is invested in overseas bond and equity markets. \par \par \uc2  ((Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41, fax +47 22 42 00 18, oslo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021217du9700vn2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
