 softer than expected -0.1 pct m/m and 0.3 pct y/y. \par \par \uc2  * German state of North Rhine-Westphalia CPI -0.1 pct m/m, +0.6 pct y/y. Bavaria said CPI fell 0.1 percent m/m in July but rose 0.8 pct y/y. Baden-Wuerttemberg data due later Mon, Hesse on Tues. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Mark/Swiss\tab      at 83.43/46 centimes vs 83.54/56 in late European trading on Friday.\par * Mark/yen\tab      at 80.05/08 vs 80.70/73 late on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Pratima Desai, London newsroom + 44 171 542 2737 fax +44 171 542 5293, uk.\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .news@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8o01ez8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
