\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  CROSS - Mark/yen falls through four-week lows. \b0\par\par\uc2 588 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 1998\par 15:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 20 (Reuters) - The mark fell to four-week lows against the yen and tested near-two-year highs against the Norwegian crown in European trade on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  As Japanese officials continued their battle against yen bears and markets continued to fret about the impact of Russian troubles on Germany, mark/yen continued to drift lower from the 5-1/2 year high at 82.80 seen last week. \par \par \uc2  "We've seen the mark hit by the fallout from Russia, too hard in my opinion. I think the economic impact is less than people think," said Gerard Lyons, chief economist at DKB International. \par \par \uc2  Last week investors who were worried about Russia's economy and finances withdrew from the share and debt markets and concerns about the impact on German banks and exporters meant the mark also came under pressure, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, Russia effectively devalued the rouble and announced a 90-day moratorium on some foreign debt payments. This development added to negative mark sentiment. \par \par \uc2  "And the yen has been talked higher by Japanese officials over the past eight days," Lyons said. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials have warned of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent days. The latest was the head of the Japanese Finance Ministry's International Bureau, Haruhiko Kuroda. \par \par \uc2  At 1304 GMT mark/yen was at 78.89/92, down from a Thursday high at 80.19 and versus 79.97/80.00 in late Europe on Wednesday. It has now fallen about five percent from last week's high. \par \par \uc2  A slowdown in Germany's July annualised M3 growth, which rose five percent from the fourth quarter of 1997 against 5.3 percent in June, dampened mark sentiment, as did a decision by the German \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to leave interest rates on hold. \par \par \uc2  The Bundesbank, meeting for the first time after its four-week summer break, set the next two weekly securities repurchase tenders at an unchanged fixed rate of 3.30 percent. \par \par \uc2  Regarding the Norwegian crown, analysts said weak oil prices are behind the mark's rise to near-two-year-highs against Norway's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Despite five interest rate hikes since March, the central Norges Bank has been unable to stem the decline in the crown. The last increment, on August 11, raised the deposit rate to 5.50 percent from five percent. \par \par \uc2  "The Norwegian crown is a classic example of a situation where higher interest rates don't help the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Lyons said. \par \par \uc2  Frequent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the crown by \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has only tempered the crown's fall against the mark, traders said. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, Norges Bank said it bought a net 426 million crowns between Wednesday and Friday last week. \par \par \uc2  The Norwegian crown was last at 4.2995/15 per mark after a session high at 4.3000 and versus 4.2940/60 per mark in late Wednesday trade. \par \par \uc2  The Norwegian crown's trade-weighted index was last at 105.82. Analysts said Norges Bank has in the past \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  or raised interest rates when this index has risen above 105. \par \par \uc2  The mark was fairly steady against the Swiss franc, it was last at 83.85/88 centimes vs 83.77/80 centimes late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Sweden's Riksbank left the repo rate at 4.10 percent. \par \par \uc2  Mark/Swedish crown was last at 4.5180/00 from a session high at 4.5400 and from 4.5420/50 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  ((Pratima Desai, London newsroom +44 171 542 2737)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8k0187i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
