\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Norway \highlight\uc2  NOK falls sharply, no sign of  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 453 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 1998\par 15:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  OSLO, Aug 18 (Reuters) - The Norwegian crown weakened sharply on Tuesday with some players pointing to a steep rise in interest rates as driving the market. \par \par \uc2  Others said commodity-linked \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were being hit across the board after Russia effectively devalued the rouble on Monday. It said on Tuesday that it would use all instruments possible, as well as precious metal reserves, to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The crown fell to 4.2805 against the mark at 1300 GMT compared with 4.2705 at 1400 GMT on Tuesday. Against the inverse European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  unit index, it stood at 105.42 versus 105.17. \par \par \uc2  Despite the decline, dealers said there were no signs of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepping in to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Norges Bank's mandate is to use monetary policy to maintain a stable crown against a basket of European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Any country with a high dependency on commodity exports is being hammered today and Norway has one of the biggest exposures with oil accounting for something like 65 percent (of exports). Norway is very vulnerable," said a London-based dealer. \par \par \uc2  Other said the move was on the back of a run-up in short-term rates. Norway's three-month swap rate jumped 24 basis points on Tuesday to 6.20 percent and now stands 70 basis points above the official deposit rate at 5.50 percent. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced a 0.50 percentage point rate hike on August 11 to support a depreciating crown and at the same time \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, buying 1.71 billion crowns between Monday and Tuesday last week. \par \par \uc2  The crown picked up slightly after the rate rise but has since slid back to levels below those seen before the last hike. \par \par \uc2  "The (\b \highlight22\uc2 central) bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is caught between a rock and a hard place. At the moment it is continuously following the market, which today has discounted another (rate) rise of 50 basis points," said a market player. \par \par \uc2  "It needs to go past market expectations, but at the same time is limited by what it can do, there is a risk they might be penalised for overkill." \par \par \uc2  Others said it was unclear what the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might do. \par \par \uc2  "The might want to wait and see if this is a spoof by the market or they might hammer it down fast. If they don't (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  or raise rates), the market might take it as carte blanche to run the crown down," said Peter Warren, chief dealer at Finansbanken. \par \par \uc2  ((Tanya Pang, Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41, fax +47 22 42 00 18, oslo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8i01050\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
