\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Norway \highlight\uc2  C.Bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to buy crowns - traders. \b0\par\par\uc2 435 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 1998\par 11:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  OSLO, Aug 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Norges Bank, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday to buy crowns to defend the flagging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The crown continued to slide in early trade after oil prices tumbled almost 70 cents on the International Petroleum Exchange on Monday due to the glut in global supplies. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said a weak Swedish crown was also adding to the downward pressure on the Norwegian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Norges Bank was not immediately available to comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk. \par \par \uc2  The crown stood at 4.2725 against the mark at 0944 GMT and at 105.29 versus the inverse European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  unit index. \par \par \uc2  It remained in a downtrend even though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday pushed up short-term money market rates by setting an interest rate of 5.40 percent for fixed-term deposits between August 11 and 13. It was the first time the bank has set a fixed rate since February. \par \par \uc2  The three-month swap rated continued to climb on Tuesday to stand at 5.91 percent at 0944 GMT compared with 5.77 percent at 1400 GMT on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the oil price slide and weakness in the Swedish crown had outweighed the effect of the fixed deposit rate. "We would have gone firmer but reaction (to the fixed rate) became marginal because of the other factors," said a dealer. \par \par \uc2  The three-month swap rate historically stands around 40 basis points above the official discount rate, which is currently at 5.00 percent. The rate is now 90 basis points above the discount rate leaving room for a 0.50 percentage point rise in official rates. \par \par \uc2  Norges Bank last raised rates on July 6 to 5.00 percent for the discount rate and 7.00 percent for the overnight lending rate. It was the fourth rate hike this year to bolster the sliding crown. \par \par \uc2  At the same time the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the first time it had stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to defend the crown since January 1997. \par \par \uc2  Most recent figures from the bank on Monday showed it net bought 213 million crowns between Monday and Tuesday last week. The bank has historically been a net seller of crowns for the state's Petroleum Fund. \par \par \uc2  "Everyone believes in higher interest rates soon," said another dealer. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far has been too small," he said. \par \par \uc2  ((Tanya Pang, Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41, fax +47 22 42 00 18, oslo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8b02va0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
