\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Norway \highlight\uc2  CB Gov:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Not Best Way To Stabilize Kroner \b0\par\par\uc2 146 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 1998\par 15:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  OSLO (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor of Norges Bank Kjell Storvik said Tuesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets may not be the best instrument for steadying the krone. \par \par \uc2  "Interest rates are the most important means for stabilizing the krone," he said. \par \par \uc2  Storvik added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not use large scale \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilize the krone. He admitted, however, that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been active in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets with moderate \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  In the month of July, Storvik said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the scale of 3.0 billion kroner to stabilize the krone. Storvik was talking at a press briefing after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier in the day raised its interest rate corridor by 0.5 percentage point. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 11-08-98 \par \par \uc2  1349GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8b06rg7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
