\par\par \b \uc2  Nordic  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 :  \highlight22\uc2 Norway \highlight\uc2  Krone Steady Late Amid  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Talk \b0\par\par\uc2 382 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 1998\par 16:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  OSLO (Dow Jones)--Both the Norwegian and Swedish units are steady to slightly weaker against the Deutsche mark in late dealings Thursday compared to their quotes at the start of the day. \par \par \uc2  At 1429 GMT the mark fetched NOK4.2720, up slightly from NOK4.2670 in early dealings, and higher than NOK4.2640 at Wednesday's close. \par \par \uc2  But the Norwegian krone's relative steadiness has given rise to market speculation that Norges Bank, the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has been in the market to bolster the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We haven't seen Norges Bank, but we have a suspicion that it might have been active in the market (buying kroner)," said a dealer with a Norwegian bank. \par \par \uc2  Although dealers conceded the krone may have been propped up a bit by some light commercial demand given its weakness, they still found it hard to believe the unit could hold up so well as it did amid negative pressures such as the weaker dollar and pound, low crude oil prices and a sagging domestic equities market, without any help. \par \par \uc2  Norges Bank's only monetary policy mandate is to keep the krone stable against other European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . So far this year it has boosted rates four times, and has periodically \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall \par \par \uc2  "Sentiment for the krone is just negative," said the same dealer. He believed the Norwegian unit will hold in a range between NOK4.26 and NOK4.29 per mark in the medium term, with a bias for the weaker end of the scale. \par \par \uc2  But in order to stem the krone's slide, the trader argued Norges Bank would have to be decisive in its actions and raise interest rates instead of using small periodic \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Only a rate hike will do if the (selling) pressure mounts (on the krone," said an Oslo-based dealer. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, in neighboring Sweden the krona (SEK) moved lower against its German counterpart, and is quoted down to SEK4.5050, compared with SEK4.4885 at the start of the European day, amid a late but mild bout of selling interest. \par \par \uc2  This is in line with its recent trend of losing ground once U.S. trade gets underway. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 06-08-98 \par \par \uc2  1437GMT \par \par \uc2  1058 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8606ntv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
