\par\par \b \uc2  Norges Bank Buys Kroner Vs Mark At About NOK4.25 - Dealers \b0\par\par\uc2 171 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 1998\par 16:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  OSLO (Dow Jones)--Norges Bank, \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Thursday, buying kroner against the Deutsche mark, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Norges Bank has been in the market several times buying kroner against the mark at the 4.2450 to NOK4.2500 levels. The volumes of Norges Bank's purchases weren't known. \par \par \uc2  "They (Norges Bank) are concentrating the buy orders on just a handful of institutions to keep it (the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) quiet," said a dealer with a Norwegian bank. \par \par \uc2  Norges Bank declined to comment. \par \par \uc2  The Norwegian krone has sagged in recent months because of an expansionary fiscal policy, a too generous wage settlement and plummeting crude oil prices. \par \par \uc2  That weakness has prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost its key interest rate corridor four times this year, in order to stick to its only monetary policy of keeping the krone stable vis-a-vis European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 09-07-98 \par \par \uc2  1413GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du7905txg\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\l